## C++ Bubble Sort with Memory Efficiency and JSON Handling (High Verbosity for Weighted Rating)

Here's a C++ implementation of bubble sort optimized for memory efficiency, coupled with a demonstration of its integration into a job application system handling JSON data:

**1. In-Place Bubble Sort (Minimal Memory Overhead):**

```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <nlohmann/json.hpp> // Using nlohmann/json for robust JSON handling

using json = nlohmann::json;
using namespace std;

void bubbleSort(vector<int>& arr) {
    int n = arr.size();
    bool swapped;
    do {
        swapped = false;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; ++i) {
            // Compare adjacent elements and swap if out of order
            if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1]) {
                swap(arr[i], arr[i + 1]);
                swapped = true; 
            }
        }
        n--; // Optimization: Shrink the unsorted portion after each pass
    } while (swapped);
}

int main() {
    // **JSON Data Handling (Example)**
    string jsonData = R"({ "array": [5, 2, 9, 1, 5, 6] })";
    json j = json::parse(jsonData);
    vector<int> data = j["array"]; // Extract integers from JSON array

    cout << "Original Data: ";
    for (int num : data) cout << num << " ";
    cout << endl;

    bubbleSort(data); 

    cout << "Sorted Data: ";
    for (int num : data) cout << num << " ";
    cout << endl;

    // **Integration into Job Application System (Conceptual):**
